on system but as far as clark  county and what we've done  we're state statutorily required i  should say  to verify the hash code on our software  to verify the hash code on all of our  systems  and everything here has been verified to  match  the certification codes that are  provided by nist for the hash code  and what the secretary of state has  instructed us to do in addition to that  statutorily here we have to create a  certification board that's made up of a  bipartisan group of  citizens from the public that have an  opportunity to participate  in our process to ensure that the votes  are being correctly counted  and there's three stages of that that's  one that happens right before early  voting starts one that happens right  before election day  and then there's a post certification  activity after the election  and in all three cases our our software  came out spotless  so we give them a predetermined total on  what we expect the vote turnout to be on  our system  and then we re test ballots into the  system and they go through and verify  that the matches  the accounts match so that's part of  what the state requires  all of our equipment here in the clark  county is federally certified for use  on the voting machine side as well as  the tabulation software  um so we've done everything correctly  we're now  performing our post-election audits  where we have to  again certify the software on our voting  machines  and also on the voter verified paper  trails confirm that those are counting  correctly  so we we do a multitude of things here  to verify that the system is correctly  working and everything is certified but  i can't ask your question in comparison  to mission i don't know what they run  next question anymore  i want to thank all of you for your  participation i kind of wish i had done  this yesterday when the group was larger  it's a very difficult job we're trying  to do and i appreciate what you guys are  doing for the community  and asking 